|~ Every value comes apart into the set of its atoms and a shape, and
   the shape applied to the set builds the value back [QSLIT#atoms]. The
   atoms are the values no verb takes further apart, null, booleans,
   numbers, strings, patterns, keywords, tag names and paths, each once, in the one
   order, and a value is taken apart to the end: the keys of its maps
   and the tags over its payloads are atoms as its other leaves are.
   The shape is a quote that reads the value back from the set by `get`,
   over a template of the reads of its parts [QSPTH#template]: an atom is
   read by the path of its place in the set, `/n`; a vector is the vector of the
   reads of its elements; a map is built from the pairs of its keys and
   values by `indexBy`, and a tagged value, the set, the quote and the
   doc and an error at rest among them, from its tag and its payload by
   `tag` [QSERR#rest], [QSSLF#doc], each of the two a quote the template runs.
   `["x" [1 1] {:b :a}]` has the atoms `#[1 "x" :a :b]` and the shape
   `~(get [/1 [/0 /0] ~(get [[/3 /2]] | indexBy ~(first) | map ~last)])`.
   The verbs are the language's own, and the test of the ring runs them
   over every example of the catalog and every literal of the
   conformance cases.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSLIT#atoms]. ~|

:any/atomKinds
  |~~ The kinds of the atoms, a word, since a recipe reads no value a
      sentence names.
  ~~|
  ~(#[::null ::boolean ::number ::string ::regex ::keyword ::tag ::path])

:any/gluedBy
  |~~ The reads of the parts of a value, the template alone under an
      empty glue, and otherwise a quote that reads them by `get` and
      builds the value by the steps of the glue.
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :glue |~~ The steps that build the value from what the template reads. ~~| /0 ::vec
    | throws :glue/NotVecError |~~ The glue is a vector of steps. ~~|
    | impl
        ~(if (glue | count | eq 0)
            ~()
            ~(:reads it
              | get {:name :get :modifiers ~(get [~(reads)])}
              | tag ::call
              | :read it
              | get [[~(read)] ~(glue)]
              | flat
              | tag ::quote))

:any/partsOf
  |~~ The parts a value that is no atom is built from, and the steps
      that build it from them: a vector from its elements by none, a map
      from the pairs of its keys and values, and a tagged value, a doc
      and an error at rest among them, from its tag and its payload.
  ~~|
  ~(:kind (type)
    | cond
        ~(kind | eq ::vec) ~(get {:parts ~(it) :glue ~(~())})
        ~(kind | eq ::map) ~(:whole it | get {:parts ~(keys | sort | map ~(:key it | get [~(key) ~(whole | query key)])) :glue ~(~(indexBy ~(first) | map ~last))})
        ~(get {:parts [~(kind) ~(payload)] :glue ~(~(tag))}))

:any/atomsOf
  |~~ The atoms of a value, its own when it is an atom and otherwise
      those of its parts, each part's gathered by the same verb.
  ~~|
  ~(:item it | if (atomKinds | has (item | type)) ~(get [~(it)]) ~(partsOf | get /parts | map ~atomsOf | flat))

:any/placeKey
  |~~ The key an atom's place is read by, the keyword of its print, which
      tells `1` from `"1"`.
  ~~|
  ~(print | toKeyword)

:any/numberedWith
  |~~ The atoms numbered so far, `{:next … :pairs …}`, with one more. ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :atom |~~ The atom numbered next. ~~| /0
    | impl
        ~(:acc it
          | get {:next ~(acc | get /next | add 1) :pairs ~(acc | get /pairs | append (get [~(atom) ~(acc | get /next)]))})

:any/intoShape
  |~~ The reads built so far, `{:numbered … :reads …}`, with the read of
      one value after them: the path of an atom's place in the set, which
      `:numbered` holds under the atom's key, or what builds a value from
      the reads of its parts.
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :element |~~ The value whose read comes next. ~~| /0
    | impl
        ~(:acc it
          | element
          | :item it
          | if (atomKinds | has (item | type))
              ~(get {:numbered ~(acc | get /numbered)
                     :reads ~(acc | get /reads | append (get [~(acc | get /numbered | query (item | placeKey) | last)] | toPath))})
              ~(partsOf | :built it
                | built | get /parts | reduce (get {:numbered ~(acc | get /numbered) :reads []}) ~(intoShape) | :inner it
                | get {:numbered ~(acc | get /numbered) :reads ~(acc | get /reads | append (inner | get /reads | gluedBy (built | get /glue)))}))

:any/apart
  |~~ The atoms of the subject and its shape. ~~|
  ::fn
    | proves :takesAValueApart
        |~~ A vector of a string, a vector and a map comes apart into four
            atoms and its shape.
        ~~|
        ~(["x" [1 1] {:b :a}] | apart | eq {:atoms #[1 "x" :a :b] :shape ~(get [/1 [/0 /0] ~(get [[/3 /2]] | indexBy ~(first) | map ~last)])})
    | impl
        ~(:held get [~(it)]
          | :atoms (held | map ~atomsOf | flat | tag ::set)
          | :numbered (atoms | reduce {:next 0 :pairs []} ~(numberedWith) | get /pairs | indexBy ~(first | placeKey))
          | :read (held | reduce (get {:numbered ~(numbered) :reads []}) ~(intoShape) | get /reads | first)
          | get {:atoms ~(atoms) :shape ~(get {:name :get :modifiers ~(get [~(read)])} | tag ::call | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote)})

:any/rebuilt
  |~~ The value the shape of the subject builds from its atoms. ~~|
  ~(apart | :pieces it | pieces | get /atoms | apply (pieces | get /shape))
